-> room

=== room ===
The Wolf’s Tavern · Room #5
The brass key says 5. You turn it over. Someone has scratched a little rail junction into the back. One line ends at the garden.
* [Follow the mark to the Secret Garden.] -> garden

=== garden ===
The Secret Garden
You find the same mark at the turn in the path. No arrow this time. What looked like a scratch on the key looks like a sigil here. The brass warms in your hand.
* [Touch the sigil.] -> junction
* [Go back to Room #5.] -> room

=== junction ===
Daddy’s Little Mortis · Obsidian Realm
The garden path becomes a rail line. Every departure board is running a Black Friday countdown. One promises “BECOME YOURSELF. OFFER ENDS AT MIDNIGHT.” Below it, somebody has painted a small arrow toward the exit.
* [Read the label in The Rebel’s window.] -> rebel
* [Explore Inpatient Corridors.] -> corridors
* [Take the exit while the clock is still running.] -> exit

=== rebel ===
The Rebel
There’s one black orchid in the Thanksgiving cornucopia. Nothing else. Above it, a gilded halo and scales of justice frame the label: “Thou Shalt Not Kill. Terms and Conditions Apply.” The placard says “Fine Print Sold Separately.”
* [Return to the junction.] -> junction

=== corridors ===
Inpatient Corridors
A door opens onto half an asylum set. The plaster ends at the edge of an uninked panel. One strip of lettering is still taped to the wall: “Collaboration continued in different directions.” A second door leads back to the same room. The exit arrow is still where you left it.
* [Return to the junction.] -> junction
* [Walk out before anyone finishes the sign.] -> exit

=== exit ===
The Exit Is Still Free
Behind you, the clock keeps counting down. Ahead, a gig bill reads NOT A TOY. Underneath, in letters somebody clearly put there by hand: FILTHY YUCK! You put the key in your pocket. “I came to hear the music.”
-> END
